Outcome: `cap_bound` — parked, neither shipped nor rejected.

The Track B generator uses the valued-reduction cycle from Example 2.2 and Algorithms 2.4/4.2 of [Chan–Maclagan, arXiv:1303.0729](https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.0729). Certificates are inverse-generated rational polynomial identities.

Verified results:

- All G1–G9(c) local gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000; exact density `1/9^73`.
- Gaussian reference: ~794,968 exact operations versus 293 for the compact cycle route.
- Fresh hardening run: every oracle attempt solved, including `hard` 3/3.
- Harness verdict: `cap_bound`; increasing cycle length would exceed the route/output cap.
- No `REJECTED.md` was created, as required.

